{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Mj7Rx1vH63wR815XKEmqjF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All clean. Here's what was implemented for R3.1-R3.4:\n\n**`cmd/tee/main.go` changes:**\n- Replaced `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` with `signal.Ignore(syscall.SIGPIPE)` so EPIPE errors are returned from writes instead of the process being killed (R3.4)\n- Replaced `io.MultiWriter` + `io.Copy` with a resilient `copyToAll`/`writeAll` loop that writes to each destination independently (R3.3)\n- Added `namedWriter` struct to track per-writer status -- when a write fails, that writer is disabled and the error is reported to stderr, but remaining writers continue (R3.2, R3.3)\n- Stdout write errors (EPIPE) now correctly set exit code 1 (R3.4)\n\n**`cmd/tee/tee_test.go` additions (4 new tests):**\n- `TestWriteErrorReadOnly` -- writes to unwritable path + good file, verifies exit 1, stderr diagnostic, and good file still receives data. Compares exit code against gtee. (R3.2, R3.3)\n- `TestWriteErrorContinuesWriting` -- bad file between two good files, verifies both good files get content (R3.3)\n- `TestBrokenStdout` -- closes stdout pipe, verifies exit 1 (R3.4)\n- `TestExitZeroOnSuccess` -- verifies exit 0 on normal operation (R3.1)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":136,"cache_read_input_tokens":63606,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":136},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bd09a5a3-e61f-4fcc-856a-0c9a1fbde06a","uuid":"c5ec8a1c-7fcc-4032-acf1-122e6d612edb"}
